## Summary

Set out to fix the TODO item "The year-calendar PDF import never names its document": `addCalendarPDF` in `tools/import/calendar.go` uploaded the school's year-calendar PDF to `/api/do/file` with only `kind`, `url` and `published`, so each new year's DOCUMENT row came in with no name (2026-2027's, `doc1vbgme8d9uv`, was named by hand).

- `addCalendarPDF` now takes the extracted school year and sends `name` = "<YYYY-YYYY> Helios School Calendar", matching the hand-entered name. It is called after `yearCalendar` has checked that the year is in YYYY-YYYY form with two consecutive years, so the name is always well formed.
- No server change was needed: `fileRoot` in `internal/db/do.go` already accepted an optional `name`.
- Left out: renaming existing documents. When the uploaded PDF is identical to one already stored, the existing document keeps its row. No real import was run, because it would fetch the PDF, call Anthropic and write to production; only `go vet` and the package's tests were run.
- The TODO item was removed.

